@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] nix-owned-files
nix_owned MUST give each tracked file in its package an owning target, so
uquery owner() maps every changed path to the graph; files without an owner
select everything (ADR-0270).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] nix-flake-attr-bootstrap-only
nix_flake_attr MUST only wrap flake outputs that have not moved to Buck2 rules
yet; it is deleted with the last flake package output and is never a
compatibility layer (ADR-0269). Its srcs are the flake's whole source tree, so
any owned change reruns it.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] tracked-files-have-owners
ownership MUST fail when a tracked file outside docs/ has no owning target,
because the affected-target selector selects everything for unowned paths
(ADR-0270).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] nix-store-import-local-only
nix_store_import MUST run locally and never upload its output, because the
output names a path in the local Nix store; it MUST forward the artifact's
declared runtime references so assembly can record them (ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;verification] assembly-refuses-undeclared-inputs
nix_assemble MUST evaluate lib.assemble over a copied tree of declared
sources only, under restrict-eval, so an undeclared Nix input is an
evaluation error rather than a silent read of the checkout. The
assemble_soundness BXL keeps an undeclared-tree probe failing (ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] go-binary-nix-parity
go_binary and go_test MUST build from the Nix-vendored source and modules in
buckCells with buildGoModule's environment (GOTOOLCHAIN=local, GOPROXY=off or
the file proxy, -mod=vendor, -trimpath, CGO_ENABLED=0) outside the checkout,
and MUST apply stdenv's `strip -S -p`, so each binary and the GitHub tools
release are byte-identical to the Nix outputs from the same pins (ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;security] npm-lock-node-modules
npm_package MUST take node_modules only from the buckCells importNpmLock tree
built from the committed package-lock.json with install scripts disabled, and
MUST run npm offline over declared sources; it never resolves packages from
the network or an ambient node_modules (ADR-0267, ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] esbuild-single-pinned
esbuild_bundle MUST use the one esbuild from buckCells, the nixpkgs esbuild
that release builds pin, and never an esbuild.install download (ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] py-static-prek-parity
py_static MUST run the same pinned ruff and ty as the precommit hook's direct
fallback, with the same flags over every owned Python file and pyproject.toml
from the project root, and MUST report every gate's findings before failing.
Its `[ruff/<path>]` sub-targets MUST run the same ruff checks on one file,
`[ty]` MUST run ty alone over every tree, and `[fix/<path>]` MUST output the
file after ruff's safe fixes and ruff format without touching the source
(ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:governance] conflict-markers-per-file
conflict_markers MUST run scripts/check_conflict_markers.exs over every
owned file, including the toolchains cell, and MUST expose one sub-target per
file so precommit checks only changed files (ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] nixos-machine-test-labels
Every nixos_machine_test target MUST carry the machine_test label, and MUST
carry nested_kvm exactly when its suite declares requiredFeatures.nested-kvm.
The macro derives both labels from nested_kvm and refuses them in labels; the
test command fails when Nix's meta.ci.nestedKvm or machine disagree,
and when a fleet variant's declared scenario files differ from its composed
test script (ADR-0270).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] machine-test-targets-generated
nix/verification/tests/machines/**/BUCK and suites.bzl MUST be exactly what
buck/machine_tests.py generates from catalog.nix, the suites' Nix sources and
fleet/scenarios.json; every fleet variant MUST have a scenario entry and every
fleet scenario file a variant. //buck:machine_tests_fresh enforces it. Each
target's declared inputs are both what selection sees and the only tree its
nix_assemble build may read.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] affected-targets-selection
tools/affected MUST select every target whose recursive unconfigured hash
(paths_and_contents) differs between base and head, plus the reverse
dependencies of every changed file's owners. Deleted files MUST be resolved
against the base graph. A changed file without an owner outside docs/, or a
change to the cells' inputs, toolchains or rule files (including the
nixos_machine_test command, buck/machine_tests.py), MUST select every
target. Selection MUST only load targets and run queries, never build an
action or a Nix derivation, and MUST report each package that fails to load
instead of hiding it.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] script-tests-run-locally
script_test and nixos_machine_test commands MUST run locally from the project
root, never remotely or from the remote cache, because they talk to the Nix
daemon (ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] bootstrap-attrs-fresh
nix/buck/bootstrap_attrs.bzl MUST list exactly the flake's x86_64-linux
package and check names; //buck:bootstrap_attrs_fresh evaluates the names
only and fails when they differ.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;security] buck2-remote-cache-optional
The execution platform MUST query the remote cache only when a
[buck2_re_client] address is configured (the untracked .buckconfig.local, or
root's ~/.buckconfig.d file on a host, present only with its identity), so
absent credentials mean plain local execution. Uploads MUST additionally
require [buck2] default_allow_cache_upload = true; the server, not this flag,
enforces that only the CI identity can write (ADR-0272).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] precommit-info-selection
A precommit check's PrecommitInfo MUST list every repository path its default
output reads in `inputs`, and its `per_file` and `shared` sub-targets
together MUST find every violation the default output finds for the files
they name; a path whose change can affect other files (a checker, a
configuration file, a CONTRACTS file) MUST NOT have a `per_file` entry
(ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] repo-check-declared-inputs
repo_check MUST declare every owned file matching `include` as an input and,
with `inventory`, the owned path list, so a change that can alter the result
changes the action key; checks that run git ls-files MUST be local_only and
never upload (ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] contract-check-per-file
contract_check MUST run scripts/check_contracts.mjs format over every owned
file as its default output, and each `[contracts/<path>]` sub-target MUST run
`files <path>` with exactly that file and its ancestor CONTRACTS as inputs.
CONTRACTS files and the checker have no per-file sub-target, and deleting a
CONTRACTS file selects the whole check (ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] precommit-selects-affected-checks
precommit.bxl MUST select only `precommit`-labelled targets, so bootstrap
flake checks and machine tests never run in precommit. For the changed and
deleted paths it MUST build every check whose result they can change (by
PrecommitInfo, or by owner rdeps and package for checks without it), MUST
select every check for a build-graph or toolchain change or --scope all, MUST
build the selection in one ctx.build call, and MUST fail naming each failed
check (ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] rust-crate-from-workspace
overalls_rust_crate MUST define a member's Buck2 targets only from the
generated rust//:workspace.bzl table, so each crate's targets, features,
editions, workspace lints and dependencies (first-party and the rust// cell's
locked third-party crates) match the root Cargo workspace; it MUST refuse a
path that is not a member and a crate with a build script it cannot run, and
binaries MUST use the Cargo profile their Nix build selects (ADR-0273).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;verification] rust-checks-precommit
Each crate's `<name>-clippy` check MUST fail on any clippy diagnostic of any of
its targets (the `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` gate with the
workspace lints and root clippy.toml), and `<name>-rustfmt` MUST fail on any
unformatted Rust source; both are `check`/`precommit` labelled, with
per-target and per-file `[rustfmt/<path>]` sub-targets (ADR-0265, ADR-0273).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build;verification] rust-leaf-parity
rust_leaf_parity_test MUST fail when an imported Buck2 Rust leaf's
executables differ from the Nix build it replaces in their set of names, ELF
interpreter, RUNPATH or panic strategy (unwind or abort), need a library or carry a `.debug_*` section the Nix
build does not, or embed (in an rpath or
anywhere in their bytes) a store path outside the closure of the import's
declared runtime references. It builds
the Nix side, so it is labelled heavy and is deleted with that build at M11
(ADR-0269).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:deployment] fleet-host-deployment-target
//fleet/hosts/<host>:deployment MUST assemble that host's enrolled
overallsDeployment bundle (the system closure plus its deployment
descriptor) through nix_assemble, so the overalls.revision it is given names
the system in place of self.rev. Its store-path output is the only bundle the
updater activates (ADR-0271).

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] nix-assemble-drv-evaluation
Every nix_assemble target MUST expose a `[drv]` sub-target that copies the
same declared sources, evaluates the same attribute with the same
restrict-eval and allowed-uris options, and writes only its derivation path:
it builds nothing beyond import-from-derivation and roots nothing, so every
machine-test assembly can be checked for undeclared inputs without running
its VMs (ADR-0270).
